Z||000006||whamel||09-27-2000||04:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by b lo 0:<BR><B>(keep that in mind next time you pull up next to a Honda</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What's that got do to with anything??  Sounds like this was two American cars!  I'm honestly not trying to start trouble here, but please don't be so stereotypical.  I met a couple of guys last night when I went out for dinner that had a very sharp Honda.  They don't street race, it's not riced out, and they were darn friendly guys with a nice clean, well done car.  I respect that.<BR>  This really bugs me if you think every single Honda is out to street race and ONLY Hondas.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Maybe I misunderstood you, but I think this whole import bias is getting out of hand here.  I know loads of Buick's, Chrysler's, Ford's, Chevy's, and Pontiacs that you would want to watch it if you pulled up next to as well!<BR>Thanks,<BR>Wade<BR>*Note - I am serious - I'm not in the mood to argue this, but it is starting to bug me when I hear things like that a lot.||||reg||1
