Z||000009||1FST2M6||09-28-2000||06:20 PM||||he was interviewed cause someone in the office of (abc) WSB channel 2 news drives a S/C Integra built by the shop. and he knew that one of the kids nailed in the "big sting" (street racing bust about a month ago) was on that same channel with his car and rear window sticker in full view. the reporter wanted to know how "the public and parents could stop the racing and save thier poor young lives" amoung other lame questions.. Ed said "the kids are gunna race no matter what you put them in... Geo Metro, or expedition.. it's up to the parents to teach them not to race except on an NHRA approved tracks with trained professionals there to help in the event somthing bad happens, but getting parents to follow through with thier "concern" is way more difficult than to just apease the kid and get them the faster car, their status symbol." amoung other things.. i'll review the tape and post it all... ||||reg||1
Z||000010||FIEROCIOUS||09-30-2000||04:47 AM||||I've been meaning to post this for quite a while it is long and a rant but I needed to get it off my chest.<P><BR>I Illegaly drag raced (almost) every night and defintely every weekend for three years! I was the fastest car in the valley. I raced a non-ricer 73 Chevy Nova with over 450 HP on tap! Let me tell you why I stopped raceing:<P>When I first started raceing it was fun and scary! My car didn't start out with 450 HP I worked on it every day. I was addicted to speed and always was looking for ways to go faster and get a better fix. I always loved that feeling after you made a few extra ponies that you could feel! I used to cruize the boulevard and made a great deal of friends. Like I said before I was out every night it was my life! I miss it to this day and unfortuneatly feel as if I am missing a part of my life! The good times I had will be never again!.......<P>The reason I stopped? the first year I raced the police didn't know me and I went pretty un-noticed but it wasn't too long until every cop in a 50 mile radious knew me and my car! <BR>I even in my last days, had a cop wait for me out side my high school, regaurdless if I was late or early, would wait until I parked my car every morning and leave, waiting for me to screw up and break a law well, after "52" tickets yes "52" You get tired of the hastle! Just to clairify; I have had four tickets for driveing too slow like eight for exhibition of speed or power and once I even was pulled over for driveing to well! (The police officer thought it was suspicious and proceeded to search my car to find absolutly nothing. He did finaly give me a ticket for haveing a burnt out licence plate bulb! after he checked the bumper height with a tape measure!<BR>Out of 52 tickets two stuck I fought them all and won due to insufficient proof and lack of the police appearing in court. In retrospect It is NOT a good idea to know the local judge on a first name basis! They even had a nickname for me in the court room, Penny. (Because I always showed up like a bad penny.)<BR>Police, if you can belive it wasn't the reason I stopped raceing! I had a pride in the way I drove I still do! I just may be the best damn driver I know! I never F'd around in the streets I raced a million miles from the nearest person it was me and the other adrinaline junkie on the road. Period! No passengers no spectators close enough to get hurt! To see jackasses on the road pullin donuts and pealing out and reving their engines infuriates me to the point of insainity! Race on a busy road with intersections? That is asking for a hot poker ramed up your ass and when you go to jail bubba do just that! All those little stupid shits gave street racers a bad name and I, I as in ME had to pay for it! Yes I raced and I got tickets because I perticipated in the illegal act of drag raceing on abandoned streets and thus made a name for myself! I never did half of the stupid ****  ALL the ricers do!<P>It seemed to me every year I raced the more stupid those I raced against became! The longer I cruised the vard the more violent the streets became! I realy don't feel that if my car beats anouther that I should have a gun pulled on me! He said it was because I lacked respect? No I beat you it is suppost to be fun, and after it is all said and done a thumbsup is all I want to see! That same kid was shot seven times the following year. He was in a car that was pulled over he crawled out of the back seat brandishing the gun. Five seconds later a life worth very little departed our existance! I was a couple of blocks away at the time cruizing, I heard the shots that night. I Was told who it was in less then a half hour by the grape vine. (street vine)<P>The more ricers on the strip the more violence I see! The more stupid lack of property and self destruction they comit.<P>Why did I stop raceing? In all my years of raceing no one was hurt until the last few months. the longer I raced the more people I witnessed act stupidly and indanger other lives! What exactly is the point of reving the engine to passer bys if it doesn't run for a crap? I mean realy does your mom know you treat her car that way?<P>It is my belief that todays kids don't have a respect for the damage a car can do.<BR>Drive a car with four wheel drum brakes no power steering no power ABS brake systems, No seat belts metal dashes and NO poof baggy to save your hinney and your level of respect may change! I've been driveing since age twelve in some form or fashion, So at the ripe age of 22 I still know squat about driveing! At age 45 I'll still be learning!<BR>We all need to stop haveing the belief that we are gods of the road! <P>Why did I stop raceing? Cause it ain't fun anymore! <P>Sorry about the space I feel better now.    ||||reg||9
Z||000011||DjKid||09-30-2000||05:46 AM||||Right on fellow Fieron.. I do say I've only street raced 4 times since I've had my fiero(my first & only car) ... All 4 times was simple, and we both I guess had a respect for one another. That neon's drivers even waved at me when he turned around. <BR>I mean its supposed to be, I outrun you.. cool.. you outrun me.. cool.. its bout whos the better driver, who got the best start, and so on.. its not bout, oh I got the bigger gun, I'd better win. the moment street racing becomes non fun for me around here. I'll stop. Right now I can't cuz my car isn't roadable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe - <A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
